{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nclaim={\\\"id\\\":\\\"C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"concern\\\":\\\"implementation_semantics\\\",\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"The command codec must carry the value length the client's configured command size permits: a command value that the client can build must either survive a marshal/unmarshal round trip unchanged or be rejected, never silently shortened.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\"],\n \\\"scope\\\":{\\\"description\\\":\\\"One command with a value of 70000 bytes marshalled and unmarshalled through the real codec, on a deployment whose client command size is configurable (aws.conf sets 1000).\\\",\n  \\\"assumptions\\\":[\\\"the client's command size is a configuration value, so larger values are constructible\\\",\\\"the codec is the only framing between a client or peer and the replica's readers\\\"],\n  \\\"excluded\\\":[\\\"the default deployment's 1000-byte commands, which are inside the field's range\\\",\\\"what a replica does after its reader desynchronises on the following message\\\"]},\n \\\"pending\\\":[],\n \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n  \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The value codec writes the length into a two-byte field, so any value larger than 65535 bytes is stored modulo 65536 while its bytes are still emitted. The decoder trusts that length, reads fewer bytes than were written and leaves the remainder in the stream, which both shortens the command and shifts every following message boundary.\\\",\n  \\\"applicability\\\":\\\"Applies to any caller whose command value can exceed 65535 bytes, which the configuration allows by construction; the shipped configuration sets 1000, so the duty is owed by the codec rather than violated in the default deployment.\\\",\n  \\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"whether the client refuses oversized commands before sending (client/buffer.go allocates the configured size, which the read did not check for a cap)\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}}\nb11={\\\"id\\\":\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\",\\\"material_id\\\":\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"symbol\\\":\\\"Value.Marshal\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":230,\\\"end_line\\\":254,\n \\\"description\\\":\\\"Value wire codec: a two-byte length prefix in Marshal and the same field in Unmarshal.\\\",\n \\\"associations\\\":[{\\\"claim_id\\\":\\\"C10-command-value-length-survives-the-wire\\\",\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Both sides of the codec read and write the length through a 16-bit field, which is what truncates a larger value.\\\"}],\n \\\"pending\\\":[]}\nplan={\\\"description\\\":\\\"Discriminator: does a 70000-byte command value survive the real marshal/unmarshal pair, or does the decoder recover a shorter value and leave bytes in the stream? Prefix: the harness builds the command, marshals it with the implementation's own codec and then unmarshals from the same buffer. Controls: the events print the declared length, the wire length, the decoded length and how many bytes the decoder consumed.\\\",\n \\\"claim_id\\\":claim[\\\"id\\\"],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n \\\"harness\\\":{\\\"kind\\\":\\\"go_test\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"In-package Go test that round-trips one oversized command value through the real codec and reports the decoded length and consumed bytes.\\\",\n  \\\"semantic_changes\\\":[\\\"harness-only scaffolding: no replica is constructed; the test calls the state codec directly\\\",\\\"the harness wraps the already-buffered wire bytes in a fresh reader, which is what the unmarshal expects\\\"],\n  \\\"prerequisites\\\":[{\\\"alias\\\":\\\"value_built\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"value_marshalled\\\",\\\"conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"declared_bytes\\\",\\\"value\\\":70000}]}],\n  \\\"legality\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The value built is one the client's configured command size permits to be constructed, and both codec directions are the implementation's own.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"One command, one value, no replica.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[\\\"the client's own allocation cap was not read\\\"],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]}},\n \\\"monitors\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"M1-value-roundtrip\\\",\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-value-roundtrip\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"value_roundtrip\\\",\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n   \\\"grounding\\\":{\\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\"],\\\"expectation_ids\\\":[],\\\"binding_ids\\\":[\\\"BB11-value-codec\\\"],\n    \\\"derivation\\\":\\\"The event reports the decoded length, whether the bytes match and how much of the wire the decoder consumed, which are the observable consequences of the length field.\\\",\\\"applicability\\\":\\\"The command was marshalled and then unmarshalled.\\\",\\\"unresolved\\\":[],\\\"conflicts\\\":[],\\\"alternatives\\\":[]},\n   \\\"applicability_conditions\\\":[{\\\"field\\\":\\\"subject\\\",\\\"reference\\\":\\\"value_built.subject\\\"}],\\\"admission_alias\\\":\\\"value_built\\\"}],\n \\\"observable_properties\\\":[{\\\"checker_id\\\":\\\"CH1-value-roundtrip\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"event_assertion\\\",\\\"trigger\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"event\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"value_roundtrip\\\"},\n   \\\"assertion\\\":{\\\"field\\\":\\\"value_matches\\\",\\\"value\\\":True},\\\"identity_fields\\\":[\\\"subject\\\"],\n   \\\"description\\\":\\\"A command value that the client can build must survive the codec unchanged.\\\"}],\n \\\"uncertainties\\\":[\\\"the check does not exercise a replica reader or the client's allocation, so the desync's effect on a follow-on message is not observed\\\",\\\"the shipped configuration's 1000-byte commands are inside the field's range\\\"]}\nq={\\\"audit_spec_version\\\":12,\\\"disposition\\\":\\\"ready_for_check\\\",\\\"preferred_check\\\":\\\"direct_test\\\",\n \\\"question\\\":\\\"A command value of 70000 bytes is marshalled and unmarshalled through the implementation's own codec. Does the value survive unchanged, or does the two-byte length field store it modulo 65536 so the decoder recovers a shorter value and leaves the rest of the bytes in the stream?\\\",\n \\\"importance\\\":\\\"The client's command size is configuration-driven, so a value beyond the length field's range is constructible; a silent truncation both shortens the command a replica may apply and shifts every following message boundary on that stream, which turns a configuration choice into corrupted replication input and reader desynchronisation. The consequence is bounded in the default deployment because aws.conf sets 1000-byte commands.\\\",\n \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\",\\\"S23-state-conflict-apply\\\",\\\"S25-defs-channels\\\",\\\"S22-replica-listener\\\"],\n \\\"contexts\\\":[\\\"one command with a 70000-byte value\\\",\\\"the real marshal/unmarshal pair\\\",\\\"client command size is a configuration value\\\"],\n \\\"event_paths\\\":[\\\"the command is marshalled, writing a two-byte value length\\\",\\\"the same bytes are unmarshalled\\\",\\\"the decoded length and consumed bytes are compared with what was written\\\"],\n \\\"activity_classes\\\":[\\\"A7\\\"],\\\"behavior_ids\\\":[\\\"B16-client-reply\\\"],\\\"fact_ids\\\":[\\\"F7-durable-bytes\\\"],\n \\\"supporting_behavior_ids\\\":{\\\"B15-durable-record\\\":\\\"another consumer of the same value codec, which shows the codec is used wherever commands are written\\\"},\n \\\"obligation_relation_kind\\\":\\\"preservation\\\",\\\"priority\\\":1,\n \\\"counterevidence\\\":[\\\"scoped to the source: the value codec writes the length with a 16-bit field on both sides, so a larger value is stored modulo 65536 while all of its bytes are emitted (S37-state-value-codec)\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the run: the local construction run reports declared 70000 bytes, wire 70013 bytes, decoded 4464 bytes and 4477 bytes consumed, with value_matches false\\\",\n   \\\"scoped to the default deployment: aws.conf sets commandSize 1000, so the shipped configuration never reaches the truncation (S38-client-command-size)\\\"],\n \\\"unknowns\\\":[\\\"whether the client library caps the command size it builds\\\",\\\"what a replica reader does on the following message once the stream is shifted, which no check exercised\\\"],\n \\\"trigger_rationale\\\":\\\"The command value codec sits on the client-facing path: the client's configured command size determines the values it builds, and the codec is what carries them into decision formation, so a length field that cannot hold the configured size is a contract break at that boundary.\\\"}\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"check\\\",\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"New obligation and its first check for a codec contract break found while reviewing the durable record's use of the same value codec: the value length is a 16-bit field, the client's command size is configuration-driven, and an oversized value is silently shortened on the wire while its remaining bytes stay in the stream. The harness round-trips one 70000-byte value through the real codec and observes 4464 decoded bytes with only 4477 consumed; the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review decide it. The consequence is bounded because the shipped configuration uses 1000-byte commands.\\\",\n \\\"plan_path\\\":\\\"plan-value-codec.json\\\",\\\"harness_path\\\":\\\"explore_value_len_test.go\\\",\\\"files\\\":{},\n \\\"candidate\\\":{\\\"rationale\\\":\\\"The obligation and binding are supplied with the check so the claim exists before the plan references it; the duty is that a value the client can build survives the codec.\\\",\\\"action\\\":\\\"obligation\\\",\\\"question\\\":q,\\\"obligation\\\":claim,\\\"bindings\\\":[b11]}}\nsrcs=[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"S37-state-value-codec\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"state/state.go\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":230,\\\"end_line\\\":254,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"code_observation\\\"},\n {\\\"id\\\":\\\"S38-client-command-size\\\",\\\"file\\\":\\\"aws.conf\\\",\\\"start_line\\\":52,\\\"end_line\\\":58,\\\"kind\\\":\\\"document_statement\\\"}]\njson.dump(plan,open('plan-value-codec.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-value-codec.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('written')\nPY\ncd .. && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-value-codec.json 2>&1 | head -8\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
